  <div class="about-box">
    <h1>Almanac of Artificial Seasons</h1>
    <p>The Almanac of Artificial Seasons is an anthology centered on simulation art, made in response to three converging forces: the deregulation of climate, the acceleration of artificial intelligence, and the drift toward neo-feudalism. These forces are already modeled, forecast and managed through simulation, from climate projections to digital twins and autonomous agents. The artists collected here work in the same medium. With game engines, artificial life systems and motion capture, they rebuild the present from its own data and infrastructure, or construct allegories that follow its logic into invented worlds. Most of this work has developed outside the art institution, in club performance, game development, artificial life research and computational comics, and it has not been gathered in one place before. The Almanac sets these works beside essays that theorize the forces behind them.</p>
    <p>Edited by Delta Ark &amp; Ilan Manouach.</p>
    <p>Partners: Src Material, Gray Area, and Fiction and Entertainment at SCI-Arc.</p>
